label Day 1
set {narcisa_s} += 5.0
You knock on Narcisa's door.
Narcisa: "Come in!"
[background arg="res://assets/n_office.jpeg" fade="0.0"]
join Narcisa left
Narcisa is at her desk, reviewing over some spreadsheets you don't recognize.
She smiles warmly
Narcisa: "So, how was your day? Not too bad I hope?"
- "It could've been better"
	set {narcisa_s} -= 2.0
	Narcisa: "Ah, well, you're still learning. It's expected to be a bit rough. You got the job done though!"
	Her reassurance is nice, but it feels like it's masking some disappointment.
- "Things went great!"
	set {narcisa_s} += 2.0
	She beamed at me, giving off the full corporate smile.
	Narcisa: "I'm so glad to hear it! I knew you were the perfect person for the job."
She smile drops a bit, her face becoming more serious.
Narcisa: "Listen, I'll be direct with you."
Narcisa: "We're behind a bit on quarterly targets. Not a big deal, but just noteworthy. A little push tomorrow would make all the difference."
She leans back, relaxing as if she wasn't dropping extra work onto you.
Narcisa: "If you could bump output by even a few percent, it'll look very good for you."
Narcisa: "The board notices initiative. And I notice people who help me keep this dump running."
- "I can increase output tomorrow."
	set {output_increase} += 0.25
	set {narcisa_s} += 5.0
	Narcisa's shining smile returned.
	Narcisa: "Ambition is a good look on you."
- "I think I need some more time to adjust."
	set {narcisa_s} -= 2.0
	Narcisa's face tightens.
	Narcisa: "Just something to think about. Best of luck for tomorrow."
- "Won't the miners be upset?"
	set {narcisa_s} -= 5.0
	set {rico_s} += 2.0
	She frowns.
	Narcisa: "I don't see any reason for them to! They're on the clock anyways, might as well be working as hard as they can."
	Narcisa: "It's nothing you should concern yourself with anyways. Focus on the end goals here.
[signal arg="End"]
[end_timeline]
label Day 2
set {narcisa_s} += 5.0
You knock on Narcisa's door.
Narcisa: "Come in!"
[background arg="res://assets/n_office.jpeg" fade="0.0"]
join Narcisa left
Narcisa has some charts on her computer, and a large mug of steaming coffee next to it.
Narcisa: "You handled yourself well today. I notice things like that."
Praise? That's good to hear.
She taps the computer screen, pointing at one of the charts.
Narcisa: "In the short time you've been here, projected profits have already increased. You have eyes on you, and this is a good thing, for both of us."
Her gaze softens slightly.
Narcisa: "How's the work been so far? Can you keep this level of effort, go higher, etc.?"
- "We need to slow down, not speed up."
	set {narcisa_s} -= 2.0
	set {output_increase} -= 0.25
	set {vera_s} += 2.0
	Narcisa didn't bother to hide her distain for your statement.
	Narcisa: "Oh, is that so? A quick reminder that I am your boss currently, not the other way around. I hope you remember our conversation, and keep it in mind."
	She lets off a small shrug.
	Narcisa: "Well, this is your court here. Do what you think is best. Just make sure to hit your thresholds if you want to see yourself here in the future."
- "Let's hit these goals out of the park!"
	set {narcisa_s} += 5.0
	set {output_increase} += 0.25
	Narcisa: "That's what I like to hear! I knew I didn't make any mistake giving you this position. We make a good team, and will continue to push this crappy site to never-before seen value."
- "It's a bit tough, but I'm managing."
	Narcisa: "Alright, keep at it then. Don't let me down."
[signal arg="End"]
[end_timeline]
label Day 3
set {narcisa_s} += 5.0
You knock on Narcisa's door.
Narcisa: "Hey {name}, come in!"
[background arg="res://assets/n_office.jpeg" fade="0.0"]
join Narcisa left
Narcisa's sitting at her desk, seemingly waiting for you.
Narcisa: "Please, have a seat. I'm glad you stopped by, I was going to come looking for you. We need to discuss something serious."
She tapped her pen on the table.
Narcisa: "There's currently a large-scale protest going on by the miners, led by someone who's been working here for decades, Randy. Everyone knows him, and trusts him, so if he's happy, they'll settle down."
Narcisa: "We need to figure out how to address this and quell the crowd so they go back to work and we don't fall behind on our goals."
She leans forward slightly.
Narcisa: "Any suggestions?"
- "We should go talk to Rico."
	Narcisa: "Hmm, good idea. If anyone knows the best way to deal with them it'd be him. Let's go see if he's in the break room."
	[background arg="res://assets/breakroom.jpg" fade="0.0"]
	join Rico right
	Rico: "Hey guys, what's up?"
	He seems a bit nervous. I wonder if he thinks Narcisa is here to scold him, with the protest and whatnot.
	Narcisa: "{name} and I, as you know, are currently dealing with the miners' protesting. As the Crew Lead, we were wondering if you had any ideas on how to solve this issue.
	Rico: "Hmm, I think you would need to talk to Randy to find out what they want. They haven't made any official statements yet, but he's a good friend of mine, so I can try and introduce you."
	Narcisa: "That could work. {name}, I'll be leaving this to your discretion. Show me you deserve this position."
	leave Narcisa
	Before you can say anything, Narcisa leaves the room.
	Rico: "Alright, let me bring you to Randy so you two can talk things through. He should be around here somewhere."
	join Randy left
	Randy: "Hey. What's up Rico?"
	Rico: "Randy, this is {name}, {name}, this is Randy. They wanted to speak with you regarding the protest."
	Randy: "Ah, so this is the person in charge? Let's get one thing straight, these conditions you have us working are not livable. My friend broke his leg yesterday, and a supervisor told him to "walk it off?" are you kidding?"
	Randy: "I've been here for over 20 years now, and each day this place gets worse and worse. You are all just powerhungry, grasping at every dollar you can make, it's sickening."
	- "I'm not like that."
		He laughs.
		Randy: "Hah, like that's true. Everyone here is in the same, working as a minion of that devil Narcisa. If I could give her a piece of my mind, I would."
	- "It's true."
		set {rico_s} += 2.0
		set {narcisa_s} -= 2.0
		He stops, seeming a bit surprised.
	Rico: "Randy, {name} is here to listen to you. We want to help, and get things moving again."
	Randy: "My demands? Half the workday and double the pay. Until then, we will continue to protest."
	HALF the time and DOUBLE the pay? Narcisa would blow a fuse if she were here. How can I negotiate this?
	- "Deal."
		set {narcisa_s} -= 10.0
		He seems shocked.
		Randy: "Really?"
		Rico: "Really?"
		Your stomach sinks. Uh oh.
		Randy: "Alright, I'll go inform the rest of the miners then. Thank you for being reasonable here."
		leave Randy
		Rico: "You sure about this? Narcisa's not going to be happy."
		I'm sure things will be fine.. hopefully.
